# Admin CMS Rules (Next.js — `admin.doublethr33s.com`)

These rules only load when editing files under `admin-cms/`. Cross-cutting rules live in `codingrules.mdc`.

## Content Security Policy
- **Single source of truth: `admin-cms/src/middleware.ts`.** Sprint 5 (Q2-20) moved to a per-request nonce + `strict-dynamic` pattern that cannot be expressed as a static header, so `next.config.ts` intentionally does NOT set `Content-Security-Policy`. Add new external domains (e.g. a new R2 bucket in `media-src`) ONLY in `middleware.ts`.
- **Do NOT re-introduce a static CSP in `next.config.ts`** — two sources would fight each other, and you'd silently regress to `'unsafe-inline'`.
- **`next.config.ts` may still set non-CSP security headers** (HSTS, `X-Frame-Options`, etc.) — those are fine to split.
- **After changing CSP**, test by reloading a protected page and verifying no `Refused to connect to` errors in DevTools.

## Auth Cookies
- **httpOnly Secure SameSite=Strict cookies** for admin session tokens. Never store admin session data in `localStorage` or `sessionStorage` (XSS risk).
- **No client-side cookie reads for auth state**: `document.cookie.includes(...)` must NOT be used to check login state. Auth is gated by middleware reading the httpOnly `admin_access_token`. If a page needs auth-dependent rendering, either gate it behind middleware or make the containing page a **server component** (`admin-cms/src/app/page.tsx` pattern) that reads cookies via `next/headers` + `cookies()` and `redirect()` or passes booleans as props.
- **`admin_logged_in` cookie** is `httpOnly: true` and exists only so `clearAuthCookies()` can sweep it on logout — never read it from the client.
- **Rate limit logins**: 5 attempts per 15 minutes per IP. Require MFA for admin sign-in (Q2-87).
- **Rate limits use the shared store (2026-07-30)**: login + `/api/admin` limits go through `checkSharedRateLimit` (`admin-cms/src/lib/rate-limit.ts` → Supabase `check_rate_limit` RPC, service-role). Never re-introduce module-level `Map` rate limiters — Vercel runs multiple instances that don't share memory. The in-memory fallback inside `rate-limit.ts` exists ONLY for RPC-unreachable degradation; don't call it directly.
- **`/api/auth/refresh` re-checks the admin allowlist** after `refreshSession` and clears cookies + 401s if the email is no longer in `ADMIN_EMAILS`. Removing an admin must take effect at next refresh, not next login — keep this check when touching the route.
- **MFA "trust this device" (Q2-92, 2026-04-29)**: After a successful TOTP verification, `/api/auth/verify-mfa` issues an HMAC-signed `admin_mfa_trust` cookie (httpOnly, Secure, SameSite=Strict, 30-day TTL) containing `{ user_id, expires_at }` signed with `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`. On subsequent logins, if `/api/auth/login` sees a valid cookie whose `user_id` matches the just-authenticated admin, it skips the TOTP prompt and sets the auth cookies directly (response: `{ mfa_skipped: true }`). Helper: `admin-cms/src/lib/mfa-trust.ts`. **Do NOT** clear this cookie on logout — the whole point is that the same browser stays trusted across explicit logouts (matches GitHub / Google). The cookie IS invalidated automatically if the service-role key is rotated, the user_id mismatches, or it expires. **Do NOT** weaken the user-id binding to a per-browser cookie — that would let a different admin on the same machine skip MFA. Stealing the cookie alone is useless without the password (cookie is httpOnly + SameSite=Strict).
- **Generic login error responses are MANDATORY** (anti account-enumeration). `/api/auth/login` returns `Invalid credentials` for BOTH "email not in `ADMIN_EMAILS`" AND "Supabase rejected password". Differentiate the failure mode ONLY in server-side `console.warn('[auth/login] reject reason=NOT_ALLOWLISTED|SUPABASE_AUTH_FAILED ...')` logs, which surface in Vercel Logs. Never widen the client-facing error to leak which side failed.
- **`ADMIN_EMAILS` ↔ Supabase user drift detector**: run `npm run admin:audit` from `admin-cms/` (script: `admin-cms/scripts/admin-audit.mjs`). It uses the service-role key in `.env.local` to verify every allowlist entry resolves to a Supabase auth user with verified TOTP, and prints `OK / NO_USER / NO_MFA / UNVERIFIED / UNCONFIRMED / BANNED` per entry. Run it whenever you add/remove admins, rotate keys, or change Supabase projects. The CEO-lockout class (2026-04-29) was caught by this script — run it before raising the alarm. Admin-gated `GET /api/admin/health` returns the same audit JSON in-CMS for logged-in admins; **never** make that endpoint public — it enumerates the allowlist.
- **Adding an email to `ADMIN_EMAILS` REQUIRES creating the matching Supabase auth user in the same change.** Use `POST $SUPABASE_URL/auth/v1/admin/users` with `email_confirm: true`, OR follow `admin-cms/RECOVERY.md`. Allowlist drift is silent — the generic-error invariant above hides the missing-user case from the client UI.

## R2 Video URLs
- **Base URL**: `https://pub-7838a3e2cbc24d59a6c4d2b2d6239bea.r2.dev/{video_filename}`.
- **Do NOT use `encodeURIComponent`** on filenames — they contain parentheses and hyphens that break when encoded. Use the raw filename.

## Vercel Deployment
- **ONE Vercel project**: `fitapp` (domain `admin.doublethr33s.com`). There is no `admin-cms` Vercel project — do not try to deploy to it.
- **Deploy procedure**: `git add` changed files under `admin-cms/`, `git commit`, `git push origin main`. Vercel auto-deploys from `main`.
- **NEVER use `npx vercel --prod` or the Vercel API** — always push to GitHub.
- **"Deploy to CMS" shortcut**: When the user says "deploy to CMS" or "deploy CMS", immediately (1) `git add` all changed files under `admin-cms/`, (2) `git commit` with a descriptive message, (3) `git push origin main`. No questions asked.

## Admin API Actions
- Every `POST /api/admin` action requires the httpOnly admin cookie + email whitelist check.
- `POST /api/ai-chat` streams to an external API — ensure no PII leaks in prompts.

## CMS → App Live Sync
- Writes to `exercises` (create/update/delete) must call `rpc('refresh_mv_public_exercises')` fire-and-forget after the write so cold-start users (reading `mv_public_exercises`) see the change. Never replace this with a blocking call — `CONCURRENTLY` is fast but not instantaneous on 5500 rows, and the iOS app already received the change via Supabase Realtime.

## Bug Intelligence UI (`admin-cms/src/app/bug-intelligence/page.tsx`)
- **`Fingerprint` and `ExportFingerprint` types must mirror `bug_intelligence_fingerprints` columns.** Phase 9 (`20260516_bug_intel_structural_fingerprint.sql`) added `op` / `error_class` / `pg_code` / `http_status` / `nsurl_code` / `endpoint` / `is_classified` / `structural_fingerprint`. Phase 10 added `auto_resolved_reason`. Phase 12 (2026-04-25) added `last_seen_file` / `last_seen_function` / `last_seen_line` / `callsite_first_seen_at` (migration `20260526`) and `severity_score` / `severity_score_updated_at` (migration `20260528`). When you add a new column to the table, extend BOTH types — `get_bug_intelligence_fingerprints` and `get_bug_intelligence_export` use `select('*')` so the API auto-passes the value, but the markdown export + inbox UI silently drop unknown fields.
- **`BugIntelExportBundle.similar_past_fixes` is populated server-side via `bug_intel_find_similar_resolutions(...)` in `get_bug_intelligence_export` (migration `20260530_bug_intel_resolved_history.sql`).** The `formatExportAsMarkdown` function emits a `### 🧠 Similar past fixes` block per report; never drop the field from the bundle assembly or the markdown formatter — it's the cross-fingerprint memory loop the Edge Function relies on.
- **`SeverityCalibrationPill` reads `get_bug_intel_severity_calibration` and renders below the title.** Migration `20260531_bug_intel_severity_weights.sql` defines the weights table + nightly calibration cron; the pill click expands to show the current weights table + last calibration window. If the migration hasn't been deployed, the pill silently hides (the admin action returns an empty array). Do not turn the pill into an editor — weight edits go through SQL `UPDATE bug_intel_severity_weights SET value = N WHERE key = '...';` per the SUPABASE_AGENT invariant.
- **Inbox + markdown export sort by `severity_score` when present.** Fallback (legacy rows): severity bucket → confidence → fingerprint hash. Never invert the comparator (`bScore - aScore` for desc) and never sort exclusively by raw severity — that loses the empirical weighting (occ × √users × visibility × build_freshness × source × regression).
- **Auto-resolution provenance lives in `auto_resolved_reason`.** The inbox renders a green pill (`auto: transient` / `auto: migration` / `auto: silent` / `auto: <other>`) and the markdown export adds a `🤖 Auto-resolved: <reason>` line. Don't gate that line on `auto_resolved_at` — the resolver can backfill `reason` without the timestamp.
- **Call-site (`📍 file:line`) is the authoritative file in the markdown export and on the inbox row.** The export wires it as `**Call-site (authoritative)**: \`<file:line>\` … Apply the fix HERE; ignore any \`Suggested file\` heuristic above that contradicts it.` Never strip that line — it is what tells Cursor to override Claude's `file_path` guess when the iOS client captured the real source.
